son merge, policy agreement required, cannot cancel someone else's, completed cannot be cancelled); LowStockTaggingTest (20 tests - the threshold rule at/below/above, zero quantity suggests sold out, syncStatusTag derivation, Best Seller preservation, manual-override detection, lowStock scope, tagging screen renders, single and bulk assignment, bulk requires items, unknown tag rejected, guests excluded, booking decrements linked stock and auto-flags low stock then sold out, cancelling returns stock, dashboard low-stock count, clearing a tag); PublicPagesTest (15 tests - landing, both service views, category and price filters, service detail with variants, inactive service 404, contact page and submission, about, admin login page, and the full 4-step password reset including that only the code hash is persisted, that the flow never reveals whether an email is registered, a wrong code is rejected, a valid code resets the password and signs the customer in, a code cannot be reused, and the new-password step is forbidden without a verified code). phpunit.xml now pins the suite to in-memory SQLite so it needs no database server. Bugs the suite exposed and I fixed: (1) Admin\AppointmentController::recordStatusChange read ->status AFTER the update, so every from_status was written as the NEW status - the previous status is now an explicit parameter at all five call sites; (2) statusHistory used latest() alone, which is non-deterministic when several transitions land in the same second - now ordered by created_at then id; (3) InventoryItem::suggestedTag() consulted isSoldOut(), which itself reads status_tag, making a manual Sold Out tag its own suggestion so overrides were undetectable - it now derives purely from quantity; (4) SalonSetting::current() created the row with only operating_hours, leaving booking_lead_days at 0 in memory (column defaults are not reflected post-insert), which made every date read as unbookable - all defaults are now explicit; (5) admin appointment routes pointed at the CUSTOMER AppointmentController because of a class-name collision, so every admin status update 500'd - added an AdminAppointmentController alias; (6) the notification dispatch map was keyed by enum value but indexed by the enum case; (7) the variant sync read an absent duration_minutes key; (8) POST /admin/tags/bulk was declared after /tags/{item} so the literal path was swallowed by the parameter; (9) six @include wrappers were missing their closing paren, silently rendering the directive as text so the inventory, terms and promo create pages had no CSRF token; (10) TermsController::create never passed the model the shared form partial expects; (11) allergies and last_services_availed had been dropped from the booking validation rules so the merged values never reached validated(). Also removed MustVerifyEmail from User, since the specified Register flow has no email-verification step and the framework was redirecting to an undefined verification.verify route. Added a 16-assertion HTTP write-path smoke test (storage/app/tmp/write_smoke.php) covering admin login, service+variant creation, item creation, date blocking, T&C version create+publish, promo creation, reports, CSV export, customer registration, booking, dashboard, appointment detail, and three negative cases (terms not agreed, blocked date, cancellation) - 16/16 passing with no server errors.
